multiflexi-server (0.1.6) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Revert 0.1.5's apps.json/runtemplates.json array_values() fix: that
    change made the server match openapi-schema.yaml as it stood at the
    time (which declared these endpoints as bare arrays), but
    multiflexi-api's spec was corrected the other way shortly after
    (2.3.3, 2026-07-15: "spec declared a JSON array, server has always
    returned an object keyed by record id; corrected the spec to
    match") - the canonical contract is now the id-keyed object
    (Dict[str, App] / Dict[str, RunTemplate] in the generated
    python3-multiflexi client), and this server's array_values() call
    was never updated to follow, so it kept emitting the now-wrong
    shape (confirmed live: multiflexi.vitexsoftware.com/.../apps.json
    still returns a bare array, breaking client deserialization).
    listApps()/listRuntemplates() now force object shape unconditionally
    (same (object) cast added to multiflexi-api's equivalent endpoints),
    matching getAppById()'s existing environment/exitCodes handling.
  * Fix JobApi::getJobById/listJobs wrapping responses in an extra
    'job'/'jobs' key, unlike every other by-id/list endpoint (App,
    RunTemplate) and unlike the generated client's bare Job/Dict[str,
    Job] return types; removed the wrapper for consistency (same fix
    already applied on the multiflexi-api side).
  * EventruleApi/EventsourceApi/UserApi: cast `enabled` to bool
    consistently on both single-record and list responses (some paths
    still returned the raw tinyint).
  * composer.json: normalize formatting/dependency ordering.

 -- Vítězslav Dvořák <info@vitexsoftware.cz>  Tue, 18 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0200

multiflexi-server (0.1.5) trixie; urgency=medium

  [ CyberVitexus ]
  * Fix apps.json/runtemplates.json returning an ID-keyed object instead
    of a JSON array (schema declared array, server emitted object).

  [ vitex ]
  * Fix RunTemplate.active returned as int instead of bool on single-
    record GET; success/fail returned '' instead of null when empty.
  * Fix AppApi::setAppById referencing an undefined $suffix variable
    (pre-existing bug, always fell through to HTML output regardless of
    requested format).
  * Remove dead StatusApi.php: extended a nonexistent AbstractStatusApi,
    never wired into any route; GET /status.json already works correctly
    via DefaultApi::statusSuffixGet.
  * Implement UserApi (was a stub, listUsers caused a 500), CompanyApi
    (was a 0-byte file, caused 501).
  * Relocate TaskApi.php from the wrong repo (multiflexi-api) into this
    one and wire it in; fix its list/get responses to match the schema's
    declared bare array/object shape (was wrapping under 'tasks'/'task'
    keys).
  * Implement EventruleApi, EventsourceApi (incl.
    testEventSourceConnection), CredentialApi, CredentialTypeApi,
    TopicApi, UserCompanyApi, UserRoleApi - all previously 501 due to
    missing concrete classes or missing OpenAPI tags.

 -- CyberVitexus <cybervitexus@gmail.com>  Wed, 15 Jul 2026 08:22:50 +0200

